      "level": 1,
      "content": "Create a List"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To create a list, we must include the list header file in our program."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "#include <list>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, we can create a list using the list keyword."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "list<string> movies = {\"Forrest Gump\", \"The Shawshank Redemption\"};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we have created a string list named movies. Now, we can use this list to store the movies."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's look at this with a complete program."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2#include <list>\n3using namespace std;\n4\n5int main() {\n6\n7\n8\n9    // Create a list\n10    list<string> movies = {\"Forrest Gump\", \"The Shawshank Redemption\"};\n11\n12    // Print the list elements\n13    for (string movie: movies) {\n14        cout <<movie << endl;\n15    }\n16\n17    return 0;\n18}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Forrest Gump\nThe Shawshank Redemption"
    },
